import crate::emit::expr::emit_expr
import redox_ast::{Expr, Ident}

-- | `over (.addr.city) .to_uppercase u` as an assignment — plan 88 leaf 3.
-- |
-- | ```text
-- | over (.addr.city) .to_uppercase u
-- | u.addr.city = u.addr.city.to_uppercase();
-- | ```
-- |
-- | # The field chain is **synthesised**, then emitted twice
-- |
-- | A `Field` node is built over `place` for each name in the selector, and the
-- | result is emitted on both sides: once as the assignment's target, once as
-- | the argument `function` is applied to. So the output is byte-identical to
-- | the `:=` form the author would have written — which is the row's whole
-- | claim, and the reason nothing here decides anything about receivers,
-- | precedence or parentheses.
-- |
-- | Those decisions belong to `emit_expr` and are reached by *going through
-- | it*: the application is an ordinary `Expr::Call` whose callee is whatever
-- | the author wrote, so a method reference becomes a method call with the
-- | chain as its receiver (plan 57's receiver-last rule, in `method_ref`), a
-- | named function becomes a call, and a closure becomes a closure call. This
-- | file chose none of that.
-- |
-- | # Why the path is emitted twice and nothing is cloned
-- |
-- | The *source* says the path once; the *output* says it twice, because Rust
-- | has no other spelling for "apply through a place". That is the same text
-- | `:=` produces and it is a place expression on both sides, so no value is
-- | moved, no `clone` is inserted, and the borrow is rustc's to judge — doc 03
-- | §2's semantics-preserving clause, which is what §1.2 of the plan makes the
-- | functional setter fail and this form satisfy.
export(crate) emit_over : &[Ident] -> &Expr -> &Expr -> usize -> String
emit_over selector function place indent =
  -- The chain, built outward from the place: `u` then `u.addr` then
  -- `u.addr.city`. Each node takes the place's span, because no sub-span of
  -- the source corresponds to a prefix of a path the author wrote once.
  mut chain = .clone place
  for name in selector
    chain := Expr::Field { recv = Box::new chain, name = .clone name, span = .span place }
  target = emit_expr (&chain) indent
  applied = Expr::Call { callee = Box::new (.clone function), args = vec! \-> .clone chain, is_dollar = false, span = .span function }
  value = emit_expr (&applied) indent
  format! \-> "#{target} = #{value}"
